# R23 The Goat's Stand (side quest, comic). By hand, polished by Gemini, unvoiced.

~ board
Narrator: An old billy goat stands atop the parish notice board, four hooves planted across the paper naming this corner the evacuation point.
the_notice_goat [neutral]: The goat chews a corner of the parish notice, holding your eye with flat, yellow indifference.
set wv_goat_met
quest the_goats_stand asked
-> menu

~ menu
* [Animal Handling DC 13] Coax the goat off the board -> moved | bitten
* [Intimidation DC 14] Stare the goat down -> moved | bitten
* [if item:wv_feast_bread] Offer the heel of the last loaf -> bread
* Ask Tamsin to move the evacuation point instead -> point
* [ends:the_goats_stand] Leave the goat to hold its post -> stand
* Step away -> END

~ bitten
Narrator: The goat stretches its neck, takes your cuff between square teeth, and gives one sharp, deliberate tug without breaking your gaze.
damage 1d4 piercing
-> menu

~ moved
Narrator: Some silent treaty passes between you. The goat steps down with the stiff dignity of a magistrate quitting a bad court, and trots toward the church.
quest the_goats_stand moved
set goat_resolved
set goat_saved
-> END

~ bread
Narrator: The goat takes the crust and turns it over on its tongue. It hops down with the brisk air of a creature that was only waiting for proper terms.
take wv_feast_bread
quest the_goats_stand moved
set goat_resolved
set goat_saved
-> END

~ point
Narrator: Tamsin shifts the evacuation notice to the well in forty seconds and one wet stamp. The goat keeps the board, the parish keeps the well, and honour is satisfied.
quest the_goats_stand moved
set goat_resolved
set goat_saved
-> END

~ stand
Narrator: The goat gives you the same flat look it gives the storm clouds, and goes on chewing. Whatever comes down Rowan's Rise tonight will have to answer to those eyes.
quest the_goats_stand stands
set goat_resolved
set goat_stood
-> END
